Stage 1 Dementia — Common Problems

Stage 1 is generally mild/early dementia, where the person can still function independently but starts experiencing noticeable cognitive difficulties.

🧠 Short-term memory loss – forgets recent conversations, names, or where things were placed.
🔄 Repeating questions – asks the same question or tells the same story repeatedly.
📅 Difficulty remembering dates – appointments, birthdays, or daily schedules.
🗣️ Word-finding difficulty – struggles to recall familiar words or names.
🎯 Reduced attention – difficulty concentrating on tasks for long periods.
🧩 Difficulty solving problems – struggles with unfamiliar or multi-step tasks.
🏠 Occasional disorientation – may become confused about places or directions.
😟 Mood changes – increased anxiety, frustration, withdrawal, or reduced confidence.
📱 Difficulty learning new technology/tasks – needs more time to learn unfamiliar procedures.
